   "evidence": "ParityOdd.lean:406-416 \u2014 `proper_covariant` rewrites `kFour_p`/`kFour_q` only to unfold, then closes with `Module.Basis.det_comp, hdet, one_mul`; `conserved_left := AlternatingMap.bilinMap_apply_left_eq_zero _ ![kFour.p, kFour.q] 1 v` and `isAlt := AlternatingMap.isAlt_bilinMap _ _`, both generic in the fixed vectors (EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/Alternating/BilinMap.lean:64,70). `gFour` is never used in the proof. Roadmap InclusiveStructureFunctions/Suggested.lean:55-66 wants `ParityOddForm V g K` for arbitrary kinematics.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Tensors/ParityOdd.lean",
   "fix": "Parameterize: `noncomputable def aFour (K : DisKinematics (Fin 4 \u2192 \u211d)) : Bilin (Fin 4 \u2192 \u211d) := (Pi.basisFun \u211d (Fin 4)).det.bilinMap ![K.p, K.q]` and `lemma parityOddAssumptions_aFour (g : Bilin (Fin 4 \u2192 \u211d)) (K : DisKinematics (Fin 4 \u2192 \u211d)) : ParityOddAssumptions g K (aFour K)` with the same proof script; keep `aFour_apply`, `aFour_ne_zero`, `existsUnique_eq_smul_aFour` and `not_isLorentzCovariant_aFour` specialized at `aFour kFour`.",
   "issue": "`aFour` and `parityOddAssumptions_aFour` (line 406) are stated only for the fixed `kFour`/`gFour`, but the proof uses nothing about either: it uses only `hf.fixes_p`, `hf.fixes_q` and `hdet`, with `conserved_left` and `isAlt` coming from the generic `AlternatingMap.bilinMap_apply_left_eq_zero`/`isAlt_bilinMap`. Since `kFour` has `g p q = 0` (its own docstring, lines 356-360), the PR exhibits the parity-odd form only at an unphysical kinematic point, and a user with `p\u00b7q \u2260 0` on \u211d\u2074 cannot reuse either declaration.",
   "line": 379
  }
